2026-09-13 22:13:23 slice 33: full conformance gap sweep (gen0 as reference
across all 537 suite tests: pass=79 / fail=458) clustered the self-hosted
compiler's remaining gaps; fixed the three cheapest clusters in one rebuild
cycle. (1) Builtin ToString had no entry in the type model: CallRetTy only
knew user-declared methods, so Console.WriteLine(c.ToString()) dispatched
the enum-name string to the integer printer and printed the pointer. The
builtin branch now returns "string" for enum and scalar receivers, matching
GenCall's builtin emission order. (2) Named arguments were parsed (sval2)
but bound positionally: Greet(punct: "!", name: "hi") printed "!hi".
PushCallArgs now rebinds like gen0's reorder_named_args -- named args claim
their parameter's slot, positionals fill the leftmost free slots, the
rewrite applies only when the bound slots are exactly 0..prov-1, and
unknown/duplicate names are diagnosed. (3) An unqualified call inside an
instance method only searched static candidates ("unknown static method
'Mix'"); with no static candidate it now retries instance candidates through
an implicit this receiver. Verified: enum_tostring and cs_b04_named_args
flip to pass (sweep 81/537, no regressions), kernels 27/27, exceptions 40x
each, fixed point gen2==gen3 at 6 361 767 bytes. Remaining clusters, largest
first: generic instantiation syntax and generic member resolution, out
parameters (enum TryParse family), real f32 storage, records, ctor
initializers with defaulted struct params (default_parameters still fails
on new Point(1), 10 vs 0).
